# Scaffold Synchronization Rule

When editing tracked Ansible role/playbook templates that are also embedded in
`cli/src/proxmox_compose/scaffold/ansible.py`, always update both:

- The live file under `config/ansible/**`
- The matching string template in `cli/src/proxmox_compose/scaffold/ansible.py`

## Required behavior

- Treat scaffold templates as first-class source files, not optional follow-up.
- In the same task/PR, keep generated scaffold content behaviorally equivalent to
  the live file changes.
- Preserve backward compatibility unless the user explicitly requests a breaking
  scaffold change.
- Validate after edits (at minimum Ansible syntax check for impacted playbooks).

## Common sync targets

- `config/ansible/roles/deploy_git_app/**`
- `config/ansible/roles/lxc_systemd_service/**`
- `config/ansible/playbooks/**` when represented in scaffold templates
